DESCRIPTION<<VER_END
PRE 4.2.0 (P3-13 server foundations): branch cut from develop to carry the server work (#239) and the deferred-item promotion tracks (#279 Wi-Fi, #280 IPv6). This commit lands the colour-coded server / client foundations on top of the network-prep train. New contract shard `contracts/networking/contract_p3_server.h` (FL_CONTRACT_P3_NETWORKING_REV bumped to 11): server / client / announcement vocabulary, host dual-role model, member registry with `{N}` disambiguation, host-global nick rules (reject when nick equals another connected member's principal or nick), and four new push opcodes JOIN_ANNOUNCE/LEAVE_ANNOUNCE/NICK_SET_ANNOUNCE/SERVER_ANNOUNCE (0x05..0x08, claimed from the free post-handshake range in contract_p3_session_wire.h). Implementation: `kernel/core/net/net_server.[ch]` (HELLO/HELLO_ACK, optional NICK_PROMPT on principal collision, JOIN_ANNOUNCE then NICK announcement per the sequencing rule, MSG_BROADCAST relay, host-driven `fl_net_server_set_host_nick` with full collision check, `fl_net_server_announce`, ordered LEAVE_ANNOUNCE on drop, kill broadcast in `fl_net_server_host_stop`); `kernel/core/net/net_client.[ch]` (state machine DISCONNECTED→CONNECTING→CONNECTED→DISCONNECTING, `fl_net_client_set_nick` reply to NICK_PROMPT, event-callback `fl_net_client_poll` decoding every announce opcode and OP_ERR); `kernel/core/net/server_bg.[ch]` (hosted-only pthread loops for both server accept/poll and client poll, plain stop-flag, `FL_RESULT_NOSYS` off-host); `userland/shell/fl_colors.h` (header-only `fl_color_announce` BLU [Server Announcement], `fl_color_success` GRN [Server], `fl_color_error` RED [ERROR], `fl_color_warn` YEL, TTY-only ANSI with `fl_color_set_disabled` for tests); `userland/command/cmd_server.c` (`server host`, `server join`, `server msg`, `server announce` host-only, `server nick -id -name` host-only, `server connected` roster, `server leave`, `server kill` host-only; `FL_SCMD_SERVER` wired into `fl_shell_cmd.h` / `cmd_registry.c` / `cmd_decl.h` / `cmd_dispatch.c` / `cmd_batch_dispatch.c`; `sh.c` createdisk-shortcut skip-list includes "server"). `kernel/core/net/net_socket.c` sets SO_REUSEADDR on bind so demos and repeated tests do not race TIME_WAIT. New tests: `tests/test_p3_server.c` exercises HELLO/HELLO_ACK, two-client join → disambiguation ("Alice {1}" / "Alice {2}"), SERVER_ANNOUNCE broadcast, host-driven nick set with NICK_SET_ANNOUNCE payload exactly matching the spec ("User <old_display> has been nicked by host. Their nickname is \"<nick>\"."), nick-collides-with-principal rejection (FL_RESULT_BUSY), and LEAVE_ANNOUNCE using the post-nick display name; `tests/manual_demo_server_foundations.sh` drives a three-pane tmux session (host + two clients) and captures every pane to /opt/cursor/artifacts for review. `tests/test_invariants.c` updated for the bumped networking shard revision. `Makefile` adds `net_server.c`, `net_client.c`, `server_bg.c` to NET_CORE_SRCS and a new `make test_p3_server` target. Replit Nix `pkgs.openssl` already in `replit.nix`; no change required in this PR. No code added under contract_p3_wifi_deferred.h, contract_p3_ipv6_deferred.h, or net_ipv6/wifi/ndp yet — #279 and #280 are still scoped on this branch for follow-up commits.
VER_END

RELEASE_DATE=2026-05-28
